      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2961919de700a07ec22a098da2a90a31?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMD-0.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2961919de700a07ec22a098da2a90a31?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMD-0.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2961919de700a07ec22a098da2a90a31?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMD-0.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2961919de700a07ec22a098da2a90a31?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMD-0.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Michael Durbin",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a45f9889d5006a6c0384",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>I suspect this is because the importer imports the container first, then the children.  Addition of children updates the modification date of parent resources.  A solution to this might be to rework the import code to do a first pass that creates placeholder nodes for everything that is to be imported and then work from leaf to root.  One should evaluate such a change in approach to see if it might also address the challenges associated with <a href=\"https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2459\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2459</a> and for performance implications.</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p>An approach that would involve less reworking would be simply to patch parents with the correct dates after all children are added when doing a lossless import. </p>",
     "created": "08/Jun/17 11:08 AM",
     "id": "19099",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/12410/comment/19099",
